<title>POLAND: KRUSZWICA JUMPS ON ERIDANIA BUY.</title>
<headline>KRUSZWICA JUMPS ON ERIDANIA BUY.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish edible fats maker Kruszwica SA jumped 6.3 percent in active trade to 31.9 zlotys on Wednesday after Tuesday's news the Cereol unit of Eridania Beghin-Say agreed to buy a 45 percent stake, traders said.</p>
<p>The French-Italian food group, which also said it sought a majority stake in the firm, agreed to pay $33.9 million for 45.8 percent of Kruszwica's shares.</p>
<p>Traders said the eventual sale had already been priced in by many investors and did not see more big jumps for the stock in coming sessions.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
